{{!
    @template enrol_apply/application_notification

    HTML body of the notification sent when a user applies for a course enrolment.

    Every label and value arrives in its PLAIN spelling and is output through a double stash,
    so Mustache escapes it exactly once. The renderer strips markup from a submitted value
    with format_string() before it gets here, which is what makes that safe: a custom profile
    field of the textarea datatype is PARAM_RAW, so a value can otherwise carry a bare "<".
    Do not convert any of these to a triple stash.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * coursenamelabel string - label of the course row
    * coursename string - plain course full name, markup already stripped
    * applicantlabel string - label of the applicant row
    * applicant string - applicant full name
    * commentlabel string - label of the comment row
    * comment string - plain comment submitted with the application
    * profilelabel string - heading of the submitted profile section
    * hasprofile boolean - whether any profile field was collected and filled in
    * profile array - list of label and value pairs, in the order the instance asks for them
    * manageurl string - link to the screen where the application can be decided
    * managelabel string - link text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "coursenamelabel": "Course",
        "coursename": "Introduction to Astronomy",
        "applicantlabel": "First name / Surname",
        "applicant": "Student 1",
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "comment": "Please let me in",
        "profilelabel": "User Profile",
        "hasprofile": true,
        "profile": [
            {"label": "City/town", "value": "Belo Horizonte"},
            {"label": "Registration number", "value": "2026-0042"}
        ],
        "manageurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?id=7",
        "managelabel": "Manage enrolment applications"
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-notification">
    <p>{{coursenamelabel}}: {{coursename}}</p>
    <p>{{applicantlabel}}: {{applicant}}</p>
    <p>{{commentlabel}}: {{comment}}</p>
    {{#hasprofile}}
        <p><strong>{{profilelabel}}</strong></p>
        {{#profile}}
            <p>{{label}}: {{value}}</p>
        {{/profile}}
    {{/hasprofile}}
    <p><a href="{{manageurl}}">{{managelabel}}</a></p>
</div>
